WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:03.320
A population of beetles
lives on dark bark:

2
00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:05.760
5 pale, 5 dark.

3
00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:09.670
In the next generation: 3 pale, 7 dark.

4
00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:11.270
No beetle changed.

5
00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:14.070
Only the proportions
in the population did.

6
00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:17.170
And no animal can rewrite its own genes.

7
00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:20.690
A mutation doesn't happen
because an allele is needed.

8
00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:23.660
So if no animal can change its own genes,

9
00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:26.960
how can a whole population
change over time?

10
00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:31.290
In this mission, you'll find out which
differences between animals can be passed

11
00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:33.180
on, and which can't.

12
00:00:33.230 --> 00:00:36.640
Then you'll pin down what
evolution actually means,

13
00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:38.580
using a jar of beads.

14
00:00:38.630 --> 00:00:43.840
Your mission: explain how a whole
population can change when no animal changes

15
00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:45.010
its own genes.
